ad and that nacho is a rat  don eladio has put a price on his head  and they plan to bring him in alive so  they can figure out who he's working for  when mike comes in gus reveals that he's  skeptical because the mission was a  success but all the mercenaries are dead  something feels off mike is more  concerned about nacho he wants to  extract him saying he's done everything  he was asked and that he deserves his  respect it's clear though that gus has  different plans and later when mike's at  home watching kaylee he ignores nacho's  call he's on the run in a foreign  country with no one he can really trust  he's made contact with tyrus who told  him about the price on his head and he's  in the middle of salamanca territory  where everyone is looking to collect the  bounty he eventually makes it to the  motel safe house after dark and if you  remember he let the mercenaries into  lalo's hacienda at 3am so he's had a  whole day of running and hiding this has  all been set up so there's a room  waiting for him he goes inside and finds  a manila envelope with money and a  handgun and there's a cell phone there  so he talks to tyrus who tells him that  it's gonna take a couple of days to get  him out of there he just needs to stay  out of sight until it's time to be  picked up and he gives him the very  specific instructions that if anyone  comes to the door shoot in this first  episode you see kim and jimmy pick up  where they left off at the hotel it's  notable that jimmy's already awake  staring at the ceiling before kim's  alarm goes off they head back to their  apartment she has her new pro bono cases  to deal with and he has to meet with the  ada in charge of the wanda guzman case  with help from the recurring character  detective roberts they've put it  together that the address he gave and  the family that showed up at court were  fake they think he ran and they don't  want to wait until his hearing in six  weeks to start looking for him jimmy  does a pretty 