ut the fire  and then calls bolsa saying that he has  an idea about how they can keep the  peace later he'll go to see hector at  casa tranquila with bolsa there to  facilitate the meeting he makes a show  of it saying that they're all eladio's  men and a strike against one is a strike  against them all and we see that when  hector reaches out his hand to shake the  look on his face tells gus that lalo is  still alive so he got the information  that he wanted and he also knows that  balsa will go to nacho's house and break  into his safe and discover that envelope  when he does we see the document inside  shows bank transfers and then it has the  number for the motel safe house written  at the bottom there nacho had noticed  that there was an air conditioner  running and a little boarded up shack  across the parking lot from his room  when he sees someone move inside he  decides to push out the air conditioner  in his room so he can sneak out the back  and then come back around and surprise  the person who's watching him the guy  makes the case that he doesn't know who  hired him or even who nacho is he's  being paid by a voice on the phone and  he's just there to watch the room and  tell them if he leaves nacho would  suspect that this is gus because why  wouldn't the salamancas have already  busted into his room so he calls tyrus  to tell him that he's thinking of  running and then he hangs up on him  eventually tyrus calls the guy's phone  who's watching and that reveals that gus  is the one who hired him nacho knocks  him out and gets ready to run but at the  same time eladio's men that balsa sent  arrive at the motel he had ducked into a  truck so they walked right by to start  kicking in the doors he spotted and he  kills one of their guys and another guy  advances on his truck shooting at him  but the cousins kill him because they  need to capture nacho alive he's able to  hotwire the truck before they get to him  and after a face-off he plows his way  out of the parking lot it's a win but  things still don't look great for him  being able to get away on his own later  we find out the truck is found but he  escaped everyone in the cartel still  believes that lalo's dead and we  actually see some cracks in gus's facade  as he's receiving the news we see his  hand twitch and then he knocks over a  glass when he's pouring some water mike  tells him that if lola was coming they  would know and that he knows he can't  make a move without a reason that the  bosses can get behind he needs to find  varga alive and get him to talk this  means that even though nacho's smart  he's eventually gonna get caught and  mike wants to take four guys across the  border to find him before they do  instead of doing that gus wants him to  go get nacho's dad and bring him there  and mike flatout says no tyrus pulls out  his gun mike closes and locks the door  and says you don't understand that's not  happening this is one of those scenes  that manages to be so tense even though  i know how the story ends for each of  the characters involved mike delivers  the line from the trailer saying  whatever happens next it's not going to  go down the way you think it is and then  nacho calls his phone he gets the  go-ahead to answer it you don't hear  their conversation you just hear mike  say that it's not his call and then he  tells gus he wants to talk to him and it  cuts away before you find out what  happens at their apartment kim and jimmy  are trying to come up with something  that will get cliff to want to set a  meeting with a potential client but then  not want to pursue the case they're  trying to plant more seeds about howard  having a cocaine problem kim comes up  with an idea that she's sure jimmy will  hate he goes to a roadside trailer that  has the inflatable statue of liberty  that was above his office in breaking  bad and is featured in the bcs opening  credits sequence betsy and craig  kettleman are inside to make their first  appearance since season one she's not  happy to see him since he stole and  returned their ill-gotten pile of cash  back then and craig's reaction to jimmy  really underlines what made these  characters so much fun their despicable  criminals who delude themselves into  believing that they're the victims and  you gotta love it after all this time  betsy still thinks that saul's the bad  one when she forces him outside jimmy  lays the perfect trap he dangles a  promise of exoneration and that he's  found grounds for a large civil suit in  their case he knows how betsy feels  about him and that she won't trust him  so he says he needs some assurances that  she won't take the information to  someone like cliff maine it's the  perfect setup he knows betsy will fire  him he throws in the idea that if she  mentions where she got this information  that he'll be entitled to a cut to make  sure she doesn't say anything and it  ends with her thinking that she's just  outmaneuvered him they more or less go  straight to davis and maine we see  another returning character jimmy's old  babysitter from his time there aaron  comes in to tell cliff that they dropped  in when he asked why they think hhm  didn't provide proper counsel betsy  offers up the cocaine addiction  accusations and craig hilariously says  that he knows this because it was common  knowledge out in the yard they sound  crazy and there's a conflict of interest  but you can see that it worked perfectly  to get clip thinking about the  accusations jimmy sets a meeting and  when kim sees that he's grabbing some  cash they get into a discussion about  the carrot and the stick jimmy  acknowledges that the stick she has in  mind is huge but he knows these people  they're more carrot types especially  betsy because she doesn't agree with his  assessment kim decides to join him at  the meeting she turns out to be right  the kettlemans are upset after visiting  a bunch of real lawyers that all reigned  on their parade he tries 