t she  lived in that house but is that what  it's trying to say at this point  everything still feels like it's on the  table in a show that always seems to  improve everything is still working it  looks great there were so many memorable  shots the performances are at a level  we've come to expect and there's an  added sense of dread hanging over all of  these meticulously planned out moves  that the characters are making i'll come  back to that complexity and how  flawlessly things are progressing in a  minute because none of this can end well  nacho's situation is incredibly dire i  can't imagine what it would feel like  knowing the cartel is looking for you  when you're deep in their territory and  you know they've got torture on their  minds there's a price on your head you  can't trust the person that put you  there and you just have to stay put  vince gilligan directed the second  episode and brought some of those  shootout chops that we gotta look at in  bagman and it's hard to imagine how  nacho gets away it's also wild to see  mike's reaction when gus tries to use  his father as an incentive it feels like  there's some real tension building  between these two characters the idea of  lalo coming north again is ominous in  that it brings kim into a dangerous  position jimmy is about to learn what  being a friend of the cartel can mean  just like mateo learned that all that  fantastic dental work came with the  price and lalo's seen enough of kim to  know that she'd be an upgrade from what  he's getting from jimmy it seems  possible that he's coming after them but  it's a lot more likely that he's going  to use them in a situation where he  shouldn't be able to move around that  easily i really love all the callbacks  the returning characters and reusing all  these objects that we can recognize you  always hear about building a world that  feels lived in and what i love about all  these things that pop back up like an  ant on a fingertip that makes you think  about jimmy's first introduction to lalo  or the h.g wells book we see in the  opening and then later on kim and  jimmy's nightstand in their room it all  makes it feel like a world where we're  comfortable where we recognize things  where we're a part of what's happening  character-wise there's a lot to parse in  what's happening between jimmy and kim  and how they're jumping into this plan  against howard the setup is there it's  put together really well it's always  impressive to watch these two work  together but jimmy committed a big  misstep when he brought up lalo's name  at the courthouse kim is driving the  action she's got her foot on the gas and  doesn't seem interested in letting up  and i feel like her pulling back in the  mesa verde situation felt like it was  the last time we were gonna see her do  something like that they've essentially  switched positions here and it's wild to  think that she's playing such a big part  in helping him transition into saul  goodman there are moments here where you  wonder if she's using jimmy to  accomplish what she has in mind rather  than working with him it's an  interesting dynamic where she could be  turning him into something she could  never be and i don't know what that will  end up saying about their relationship  mike pocketed the fake id for nacho's  father he's testing what he can get away  with saying in front of his boss and  it's rare to see gus showing signs that  the situation is getting to him with all  the darkness that surrounds the coming  ending it's a treat that the show still  manages to take time to be extremely  funny when it wants to be the way jimmy  turns things around at the country club  is probably where i laughed the most  based on the situation they created  there but the whole existence of these  kettleman characters brought it to a  similar place in the second episode  betsy's inability to see that they are  actually criminals or at least to admit  as much will always work for me and  craig is just the perfect compliment and  i mentioned how things were working out  pretty flawlessly to this point gus is  able to plant evidence that balsa finds  lalo is able to buy time by having a  body double around and jimmy and kim are  thinking ahead and don't seem like they  can miss the thing is is that howard  should suspect jimmy planted these drugs  or whatever happens to him just a couple  of days ago he confronted kim at the  courthouse telling her about all the  deranged stuff that jimmy's doing this  leads me to believe that they know  howard will figure this out and that's  all part of their plan but you also have  to expect that all these things that we  see getting set up here are going to  start falling apart so it's an exciting  place to be i'm looking forward to see  where they go next what happens when  that awful woman with the ponytail is  driving where this thing will end up and  i think that's a good place to leave  things let me know in the comments what  you thought about these first two  episodes what you thought about the  teaser what it says about what happened  to saul and what you're hoping to see in  the next couple of episodes please like  this video if you enjoyed it please  subscribe to my channel if you haven't  already and thanks for watching i'll  talk to you soon
 

